+## Publication and recovery
+
+Both generated XMLs are validated, flushed, closed and read back before a
+same-directory selector replacement activates them. Failed writes/registrations
+retain the previous complete pair. A per-root lock serializes publishers across
+processes. Unchanged output reuses its generation. Existing generation contents
+are never repaired in place. The last-good selector journal is runtime-scoped;
+a different game version cannot restore its cached XMLs. Unknown custom INI
+content is preserved and loading fails with a diagnostic. Recognized unsafe
+legacy or damaged managed selectors are restored from a valid journal or made
+neutral before reading the base files. A valid previous pair can remain active
+if new startup validation fails.
